cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Protein Function Rescue: structure-based rediscovery of hypothetical proteins from the AlphaFold Database"
abstract: >-
  A transparent, dependency-light pipeline that mines an AlphaFold Protein Structure Database proteome
  for unannotated ("hypothetical"/"uncharacterized") proteins whose 3D structure matches a protein of
  known function, characterises their binding pockets, verifies conserved catalytic residues, and ranks
  the resulting candidate function assignments. It runs on commodity hardware (no GPU, no HPC) using
  native TM-align and geometric pocket back-ends, with optional Foldseek/fpocket back-ends for scale.
  Includes an interactive web viewer and a leave-one-out validation benchmark.
